+ * unbuilt term? Read-only: nothing is forced, copied or changed. True only for
+ *   - two references to one stored value (one Box, no substitution pending on either);
+ *   - two references to one definition (V_GLOBAL, the same id);
+ *   - two words of one value; two constructor cells of one constructor whose parts are the same;
+ *     two pairs whose parts are the same;
+ *   - an unbuilt subterm (V_THUNK, no substitution pending) is read as its record's syntax in its
+ *     environment, when the record is a function of its inputs alone (record_fresh, lang.c: no %var,
+ *     %dim, memory, foreign call or observation of sharing is reached from its syntax); two pieces
+ *     of syntax are the same when they are one piece in the same environments, or have the same
+ *     head (a call, a constructor, a pair, an application, a projection, a word, ...) and the same
+ *     parts; syntax and a value are the same when the value is what the syntax builds, part by part;
+ *   - two deferred calls (V_DEFER of O_CALL) of one definition that is a function of its inputs
+ *     alone (global_fresh) whose arguments are the same.
+ * Sound because each case is a congruence: the machine is deterministic, so one code built twice on
+ * the same inputs gives the same value, and conversion is reflexive on it. Assumed of the caller
+ * (lib/check.cub, conv-data and uconv): no λ whose code makes fresh names is a part of the values
+ * compared (a part that is a λ is the same only as one stored value). Every other kind (another
+ * deferred operation, a λ, a neutral, a part not yet there) answers false, and the caller compares
+ * as before. The budget bounds the cells looked at. Only when one thread
